<h1>finite state transducer</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="finiteStateMachine.html"><em>finite state machine</em></a> specifically with a read-only input and a write-only output.  The input and output cannot be reread or changed.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="turingTransducer.html"><em>Turing transducer</em></a>, <a href="pushdownTransducer.html"><em>pushdown transducer</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Thanks to L. J. Buitinck for correcting the definition.  28 May 2004.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

